                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='12'>Join Structure:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>The two sheets from the data.xlsx file — Products and Dynamic — were joined using an inner join on the Brand field. This join ensures that only records present in both tables are included in the visualisations.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Join key: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Brand</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Join type: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Inner join</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>This join was applied during data source setup in Tableau before building the dashboards.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='12'>Connection Type:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Manual import</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='12'>Calculation Notes:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• MoM and Buyout Rate are calculated using manually aggregated expressions</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• Custom parameters are used for dynamic filtering</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='13'>3. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Why is the KPI indicator not showing data for the selected brand?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>The brand’s sales volume might be too small to register on the scale of the chart. The value may be rounded visually to zero — this applies to both revenue and unit sales.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Why do values on the charts differ from the table values?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Charts display aggregated and rounded data, while tables reflect precise values. In addition, some charts may show only top-performing categories or brands, whereas tables list the full dataset.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='13'>4. Dashboard Structure</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Top section:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> KPI blocks (Revenue, Sales, Average Buyout Rate)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Line plots:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> Metric dynamics over months</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Bar chart:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> Top products by average price in the current month</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Table:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> Breakdown by brand, category, and product</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Scatter plot:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> Relationship between average price and buyout rate</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Pie charts:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> Revenue shares by category and country with dynamic grouping</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Map:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> Average product price by country for the current month</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Bubble chart:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> Sales volume by brand</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='12'>Filters available for:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• Category</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• Brand</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• Country</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#f5f5f5' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>• Month</run>
                  </formatted-text>
